{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpQ4pC98cZTHAJW97SRSWV","type":"tool_result","content":"303\t---\n304\t\n305\t## 11. Decision log / learnings\n306\t\n307\t### c001 — REJECTED (STATIC_CHECK_FAILED, no GPU run)\n308\t- Error: `computational torch operators are forbidden in the submitted path`.\n309\t- Root cause: `run()` used `flat = topk_idx.reshape(-1).contiguous()` and\n310\t  `flat = flat.to(torch.int32)`. The evaluator's **static allowlist** rejects `.contiguous()` and\n311\t  `.to()`/dtype-cast as \"computational\" torch ops — even though they are plumbing in intent. The\n312\t  kernels themselves were never reached; this is a pure host-side plumbing rejection, not a kernel\n313\t  bug and not a stability/prefix defect.\n314\t- **New constraint discovered (applies to all future candidates):** the submitted `run()` path may\n315\t  use only the narrowest tensor plumbing. Confirmed-forbidden so far: `.contiguous()`, `.to(dtype)`.\n316\t  Safe-so-far plumbing to rely on: `torch.empty`, `torch.zeros` (allocation), `.reshape(-1)` /\n317\t  `.view(-1)` (shape view), `.numel()`, `.device`, Triton launch/grid math. Do **not** cast dtype or\n318\t  call `.contiguous()` in `run()`.\n319\t- **c002 fix (next candidate):** identical kernels to c001, but strip the two offending calls:\n320\t  - Flatten with a pure view: `flat = topk_idx.reshape(-1)` (input from `torch.randint(...,\n321\t    dtype=int32)` is already contiguous int32, so no cast/contiguous needed). Match reference\n322\t    exactly, which also just does `topk_idx.reshape(-1)`.\n323\t  - Keep everything else (atomic hist K1 + cumsum K2 + S1 scatter K3, `BLOCK=1024`, `num_warps=4`).\n324\t  - This is the first candidate expected to actually reach the GPU and report per-workload\n325\t    correctness + speedup; it is the true correctness baseline for the trunk.\n326\t- Note: if a later workload ever delivers a non-int32 / non-contiguous input and a cast is truly\n327\t  required, it must be done **inside a Triton kernel** (e.g. load + cast in-kernel), never via a\n328\t  host-side torch computational op. Not expected here (spec fixes int32 contiguous input).\n329\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7604146c-ed96-4f13-996e-fef77b8439f9","uuid":"3a495db0-a40d-44bb-9df4-ef3fff411f7e","timestamp":"2026-09-16T18:09:49.098Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-058_moe_expert_token_radix_sort_with_prefix_sum/docs/plan.md","content":"---\n\n## 11. Decision log / learnings\n\n### c001 — REJECTED (STATIC_CHECK_FAILED, no GPU run)\n- Error: `computational torch operators are forbidden in the submitted path`.\n- Root cause: `run()` used `flat = topk_idx.reshape(-1).contiguous()` and\n  `flat = flat.to(torch.int32)`. The evaluator's **static allowlist** rejects `.contiguous()` and\n  `.to()`/dtype-cast as \"computational\" torch ops — even though they are plumbing in intent. The\n  kernels themselves were never reached; this is a pure host-side plumbing rejection, not a kernel\n  bug and not a stability/prefix defect.\n- **New constraint discovered (applies to all future candidates):** the submitted `run()` path may\n  use only the narrowest tensor plumbing. Confirmed-forbidden so far: `.contiguous()`, `.to(dtype)`.\n  Safe-so-far plumbing to rely on: `torch.empty`, `torch.zeros` (allocation), `.reshape(-1)` /\n  `.view(-1)` (shape view), `.numel()`, `.device`, Triton launch/grid math. Do **not** cast dtype or\n  call `.contiguous()` in `run()`.\n- **c002 fix (next candidate):** identical kernels to c001, but strip the two offending calls:\n  - Flatten with a pure view: `flat = topk_idx.reshape(-1)` (input from `torch.randint(...,\n    dtype=int32)` is already contiguous int32, so no cast/contiguous needed). Match reference\n    exactly, which also just does `topk_idx.reshape(-1)`.\n  - Keep everything else (atomic hist K1 + cumsum K2 + S1 scatter K3, `BLOCK=1024`, `num_warps=4`).\n  - This is the first candidate expected to actually reach the GPU and report per-workload\n    correctness + speedup; it is the true correctness baseline for the trunk.\n- Note: if a later workload ever delivers a non-int32 / non-contiguous input and a cast is truly\n  required, it must be done **inside a Triton kernel** (e.g. load + cast in-kernel), never via a\n  host-side torch computational op. Not expected here (spec fixes int32 contiguous input).\n","numLines":27,"startLine":303,"totalLines":329}}}
